hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16060","He said, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, meaning Ibn Urwah, he said, my father informed me, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from an uncle of his called Jariyah ibn Qudamah, that a man said to him, O Messenger of Allah, say to me a saying, and make it brief upon me, that I may understand it. He said: Do not anger. So he repeated upon him many times, each of that saying, do not anger. Yahya said, thus said Hisham, I said, O Messenger of Allah, while they say he did not meet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
